>     # elites, sigma floor, Z[0] = mu, 6 iterations) run on a block of BS seeds at once, so each iteration does ONE
>     # predict/gather/sync for BS*K states instead of BS small ones.  CEM is CPU/launch-bound (numpy propagation + a GPU sync
>     # per call), and on CUDA (K=384, ~54k seed caps, seeds ready only at ~0.8 B) the per-seed loop is cut by ref_deadline,
>     # so a faster loop refines more seeds.  Results differ from the per-seed loop only through the RNG stream.
